+  - **Facts extension (S-1, B.2).** The check file gets one value probe (runner `semantic/checkFile.ts`, `generateCheckFile(imports, decls, { valueConsts: { library } })`; `refresh.ts` always asks for it).
+    - It imports `Lean.CoreM` and `Lean.Util.FoldConsts` after the model's modules, not the whole of `import Lean`: the same API, at a fraction of the cost. Peak RSS on a scratch build of the Spyro fixture, `/usr/bin/time` under `capped.sh` (the check alone, `lake env lean --stdin --json`): 466,276 kB and 0.20 s before; 554,868 kB and 0.30 s with the probe; 1,608,556 kB and 15.6 s with `import Lean` (measured, not used). The other probes' messages are byte-identical, two lines further down.
+    - One `#eval` (a CoreM action) prints one JSON line, `{"telelean-value-consts":[…]}`, one entry per probed declaration in order: `Expr.getUsedConstants` of the value of a definition, theorem or opaque (`[]` for an axiom, inductive, constructor …; `null` for a name Lean does not know). A constant of the model library that is not probed itself (`_proof_1`, `match_1`, an equation lemma, a private or derived declaration) is replaced by its own value's constants, transitively; constants outside the library are left out. So every listed name is a declaration of the facts. The names reach Lean as one JSON-escaped string literal, split into components there (never parsed as syntax).
+    - `DeclFacts.valueConsts?: string[]` (core `facts.ts`; nothing else bumped; facts without it load). An error inside the `#eval`, no output or an unreadable line voids the probe for every declaration (`CheckOutput.valueProblems`, so the facts say `check-errors` with the reason); the other probes are unaffected.
+    - Known limit: a model that declares a name that the modules `Lean.CoreM` imports also declare would now fail the check file's imports, and so get no facts at all (its declarations would have to live in a namespace such as `Lean` or `Std`; noted, not handled). Handled since: see the fixer 1d entry below.
